{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-26T18:17:26.704Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_instance":"1cfc0cbf75050fc488823206","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-26T18:17:26.704Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"Confirmed upstream SDK recovery regression in 2026.10.23. The Node 26 CI test SIGKILL during root write leaves the previous budget and transcript intact fails with lock_conflict, reason lock_owner_dead, after roughly 3040 ms. Node 22 reaches only the separate changelog drift. A deterministic minimal SDK repro confirms that the commit fence leaves a cleanup gate that outlives the default 3000 ms wait; dead-owner takeover succeeds once the gate expires. The 2026.10.23 changelog documents new fencing (GH-1549), but does not document removal or delay of dead-owner recovery. Do not hide this behind package retries, longer test waits, skipped tests, or lowered coverage.\n\nMinimal reproduction, run as a module in a package with SDK 2026.10.23 installed:\n```js\nimport { mkdtempSync, writeFileSync, rmSync } from 'node:fs';\nimport { tmpdir } from 'node:os';\nimport { fork } from 'node:child_process';\nimport { join } from 'node:path';\nimport { pathToFileURL } from 'node:url';\nimport { createRequire } from 'node:module';\nconst require = createRequire(join(process.cwd(), 'package.json'));\nconst sdkUrl = pathToFileURL(require.resolve('@unbrained/pm-cli/sdk')).href;\nconst { acquireLockLease, isPmCliExpectedError } = await import(sdkUrl);\nconst root = mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'pm-fence-repro-'));\nconst childPath = join(root, 'writer.mjs');\nwriteFileSync(childPath, `\nconst { acquireLockLease } = await import(${JSON.stringify(sdkUrl)});\nconst lease = await acquireLockLease(${JSON.stringify(root)}, 'repro-item', 1, 'writer', false, false, 0);\nawait lease.fence(async () => {\n  setInterval(() => {}, 1000);\n  process.send('fenced');\n  await new Promise(() => {});\n});\n`);\nconst child = fork(childPath, {stdio:['ignore','ignore','inherit','ipc']});\ntry {\n  await new Promise((resolve,reject) => { child.once('message',resolve); child.once('error',reject); child.once('exit',code=>reject(new Error('writer exited '+code))); });\n  const exited = new Promise(resolve => child.once('exit',resolve));\n  child.kill('SIGKILL');\n  await exited;\n  await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 1200));\n  let started = Date.now();\n  try {\n    const lease = await acquireLockLease(root, 'repro-item', 1, 'reader', false, false, 3000);\n    await lease.release();\n    console.log('early takeover succeeded',Date.now()-started);\n  } catch(error) {\n    console.log(JSON.stringify({code:error.code,reason:isPmCliExpectedError(error)?error.context.reason:undefined,elapsed_ms:Date.now()-started}));\n  }\n  await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve,10500));\n  started=Date.now();\n  const lease = await acquireLockLease(root, 'repro-item', 1, 'reader', false, false, 3000);\n  await lease.release();\n  console.log('takeover after gate expiry succeeded',Date.now()-started);\n} finally { child.kill('SIGKILL'); rmSync(root,{recursive:true,force:true}); }\n```\nObserved: {\"code\":\"lock_conflict\",\"reason\":\"lock_owner_dead\",\"elapsed_ms\":3029}; the identical acquisition succeeds after gate expiry. The reproduction sends its readiness message from inside lease.fence and keeps the child alive until SIGKILL. It uses only a synthetic tracker and removes its own scratch directory. Existing production code is preserved; the uncommitted retry wrapper and tests are retained outside the package for review only."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-26T18:17:26.704Z"}],"before_hash":"7a3219f2e54613e4382188250b8273d4de60e1a829f5d1b76f3e0d0d8158c3ae","after_hash":"29134a6054ce33a7c904abd389f82094c8d8b8f7c90fa2801bf31c09e8aa2a75","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"5b2dfd5984e9a1d3ec31ba976e693a2a73bd4104b1db97de22ee443d9547795f"}
